\paragraph{Limited architectural diversity.}
Three of four tested models (OT-7B, R1-32B, QwQ-32B) share the Qwen-2.5 architecture. The addition of OT-7B (Qwen, 7B, STILL-trained) partially resolves the architecture-scale confound: both 7-8B models show HS advantages despite different architectures, supporting scale as the primary moderator. However, we lack a Llama-32B model to fully disentangle architecture from scale effects. Evaluation on additional architectures (e.g., Mistral, Gemma) and intermediate scales (13B, 70B) is needed to confirm the scale-dependent pattern.

\paragraph{OT-7B embedding layer anomaly.}
OT-7B's best probe layer is the embedding layer (layer 0, 0\% depth), an unusual result given that all other models select transformer layers at 3--44\% depth. The best transformer layer for OT-7B is layer 16 (57\% depth). We do not have a satisfying explanation for why embedding-level features outperform transformer representations on this model. This anomaly warrants investigation with additional STILL-trained models to determine whether it reflects a property of the training method or is specific to this model.
